---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";
---
<Layout title="A pediatrician in Blacksburg | Kin & Campus" description="A board-certified pediatrician in Blacksburg for Virginia Tech students. Refills, sick visits, and forms, coordinated with the hometown doctor.">
<div class="w hero2"><div><div class="eyebrow">Blacksburg</div><h1>Someone looking after them.</h1><p class="lead">A board-certified physician right here in Blacksburg, looking after them the years they are away from you on campus.</p><p class="hero-cta"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a><a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>For parents &rarr;</a><a class="lnk" href={href("students")}>For students &rarr;</a></p></div>
<img class="art" src={href("photos/drillfield-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="Fall leaves on the Drillfield, Burruss Hall across the green">
</div>
<div class="w"><div class="trust"><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg><b>The plan stays on</b><span>Refills and chronic care continue here, including holidays and finals.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><b>Close enough to see them</b><span>Eight minutes from campus. We can usually see them the same week, and often the same day.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg><b>You stay in the loop</b><span>If they agree, we keep you and their hometown doctor informed.</span></div></div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><div><div class="eyebrow">For parents</div><h2>They're far from home. We are local.</h2><p>Most parents call about the same things. ADHD or anxiety medication that cannot lapse. An inhaler. A sick day. A housing or sports form.</p><p>We take that from the doctor who has known them since kindergarten, and we keep it going here.</p><p><a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>How we look after them &rarr;</a></p></div>
<svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 600 190" role="img" aria-label="You, Kin and Campus, and your student, connected"><path d="M112 80Q190 10 265 66M335 66Q410 10 488 80" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="2 10" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="70" cy="82" r="42" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="70" cy="70" r="12" fill="#F6EFE4"/><path d="M46 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#F6EFE4"/><circle cx="530" cy="82" r="42" fill="#C9A24B"/><circle cx="530" cy="70" r="12" fill="#2A1A1E"/><path d="M506 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#2A1A1E"/><circle cx="300" cy="78" r="40" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M272 84L300 58 328 84v22H272z" fill="#FBF7F0" stroke="#6B2737" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="293" y="90" width="14" height="16" fill="#C9A24B"/><g font-family="DM Sans,sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle"><text x="70" y="150">You</text><text x="300" y="150">Kin &amp; Campus</text><text x="530" y="150">Your student</text></g></svg></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">While they are here</div><h2>This is the work.</h2>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Their plan</h3><p>Whatever they already take, we keep it going. Asthma, ADHD, anxiety medication. We tell you if something changes.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>A doctor nearby</h3><p>A pediatrician who lives in Blacksburg. Close enough to see them when they are actually sick.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>How to take care of themselves</h3><p>College is when they start doing this without you. We show them how: appointments, refills, when to ask for help.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Everyone on the same page</h3><p>Student, physician, parents, and the hometown doctor. We talk it through, then we write it down.</p></div>
</div></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Once you join</div><h2>A parent starts. The student keeps the number.</h2>
<ol class="steps">
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><h3>You write us</h3><p>Tell us who is heading to Blacksburg. We set up a call. Nothing clinical goes on this website.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><h3>They meet their doctor</h3><p>A first visit in town, before classes get loud.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><h3>The number is theirs</h3><p>They text when something comes up. We check in around midterms and holidays.</p></div></li>
</ol></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h2>Privacy respected. Parents kept in the loop.</h2><p>At 18 the chart is theirs. Before we start, we write down what they want shared with you. We follow that. Their hometown doctor still gets a note the same day if the plan changes. <a class="lnk2" href={href("privacy")}>How sharing works &rarr;</a></p></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><h2>What this looks like.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>For your student</h3><p>A doctor in Blacksburg who treats them like an adult. A text when something comes up.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>For you</h3><p>Someone here who knows the plan, and who will call you when you asked to be called.</p></div></div>
<p class="cite" style="max-width:640px;margin-top:28px">An ER visit can cost hundreds of dollars, or several thousand on a high-deductible plan. If it is a true emergency, call 911. Large-employer plans averaged $646 out of pocket. <a href="https://www.kff.org/health-costs/emergency-department-visits-exceed-affordability-threshold-for-many-consumers-with-private-insurance/">KFF / Peterson-Kaiser Health System Tracker</a>, 2019 claims (published 2022).</p>
<p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
